{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1013981-is-it-possible-to-pass-through-the-changeling-way-during-adulthood-nowadays","id":1013981,"title":"Is it possible to pass through the Changeling Way during adulthood nowadays?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-07T14:30:13-08:00","id":1013981,"title":"Is it possible to pass through the Changeling Way during adulthood nowadays?","content":"Hey!<br /> I'm conceiving a new chronicle where the characters are going to start as normal humans (unconsciously possessing faerie blood) that have accidentaly passed through a Trod. During their journey through the Dreaming they're going to deal with a lot of chalenges that somehow will show them that life is hard and full of sorrows, then, if they succed and reach the final point, they're going to find a magnificent cortege with gorgeous people made of pure dreams, light and beauty. The court'll say to them that they were actually convoking them. <br /> At this moment, they'll offer them an odd deal.<br /> As living is all about sorrow, pain, death and losses, they're all willing to freed the characters from those things. They'll offer this deal: the characters can live forever, young and far from all those things that've hurt them somehow. To complete this gift, they must leave their old lives. Their bodies and memories will be left behind, and those wonderful creatures will carry their burden of living, dressing their bodies and memories and suffering all those afflictions of living instead of those blessed characters.<br /> <br /> Or this is how they'll try to present this contract.<br /> <br /> <br /> The question is: is it possible to an adult or young character pass through the Changeling Way nowadays?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T15:36:47-08:00","id":1014017,"title":"","content":"If that's the idea you are using for your game, then absolutely. I'm not sure if there's any mechanics to support it, but it sounds like a great start of a game to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T02:14:31-08:00","id":1014216,"title":"","content":"It seems Arcadian SIdhe did that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T04:18:35-08:00","id":1014240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1013981-is-it-possible-to-pass-through-the-changeling-way-during-adulthood-nowadays?p=1014216#post1014216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems Arcadian SIdhe did that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know since this term is new to me (I heard it for the first time when they announced C20).<br /> <br /> I'm designing the challenges and'll post here soon.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if a Changeling who passes through this process needs to pass through Chrysalis after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T05:14:31-08:00","id":1014252,"title":"","content":"There are two ways you can do this with the RAW:<br /> <br /> 1. This *is* their chrysalis. A bunch of adults who should've awoken already are called to the Dreaming to finally see their true selves and return as fae.<br /> <br /> 2. These humans are being asked to give up their mortal bodies in exchange for immortality in Acadia. The players can then either continue as mortals in an alien fantasy realm or play the sidhe who take their bodies. <br /> <br /> Both are possible, although the latter is closer to what you propose. The latter is also how Arcadian Sidhe (literally sidhe from Arcadia) are given human forms. According to Time of Judgement, the displaced human souls might not get a great deal, but that's an optional sourcebook anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T06:11:54-08:00","id":1014268,"title":"","content":"Actually I kind of love the idea of &quot;not a great deal in truth&quot;, as presented in ToJ and DotD (Keremet). This intro is just to show faeries as something more unpredictable, with their own purposes and their own interpretation of the word Fair.<br /> <br /> Do the Arcadian Sidhes keep the feelings and emotions about the things and people that body used to feel before? I still don't want those characters to be something new (as the players worked so hard conceiving them), I want exactly what a Chrysalis does: you are something different, but partially still the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T08:18:46-08:00","id":1014320,"title":"","content":"yes its 